    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45">

                <pb facs="0103" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg29"/>

                <head>Mr. Burnley to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 28, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to your note of the 14th
                    instant, relating to suspicions entertained that two vessels in course of
                    construction in Montreal are intended <pb facs="0104" n="30" xml:id="pg30"/> to
                    be employed for purposes hostile to the United States, I have the honor to
                    transmit to you herewith copy of a despatch which I have received from the
                    governor general of Canada, by which you will perceive that his excellency will
                    cause an investigation to be made.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. HUME BURNLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d45-a1.xml" xpointer="d45-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
